      "message": "`vma_pgoff_pages()` looks like the right length, thanks.\n\nOne more case: the exact lookup only checks `vm_pgoff`, so a 4KB process could mmap at the fake offset + 4KB..12KB (`vm_slice_off` 1..3) and still match. The GEM fault handlers index the object with `(address - vm_start) \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT` and ignore the slice (shmem helper, TTM), while `insert_pfn()` does add it, so I think the process would get the wrong pages.\n\nSince GEM offsets are always page aligned, could we return `-EINVAL` for a non-zero `vma_slice_off(vma)` before the lookup, as `perf_mmap()` does?",
